<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Patch>

	<!--
		The succubus gains Alpha Genes' medium armour and the hellguard gains its major armour.
		Both already carry a Big and Small armour gene, so this stacks a second one on top rather than replacing
		anything, which is why it sits with the rebalances rather than the convergence patches.

		Gating, which is why this is its own folder: the two demon xenotypes are not Heaven and Hell or Vampires and
		the Undead defs. Big and Small - Genes &amp; More defines them, inside a folder its own LoadFolders only loads
		when RedMattis.Undead or RedMattis.Heaven is active. This folder mirrors that exact condition, which is also
		what the original any-of mod check came to.
		The Alpha Genes side sits in a subfolder gated on it in loadFolders.xml.

		Verified against Genes &amp; More 1.6: the succubus lists BS_ToughSkin and the hellguard lists BS_NaturalArmor,
		and neither already lists the Alpha Genes gene, so both adds land.
		Each add skips a xenotype that already has the gene. Fix 2026-10-31 (player report: "Hyperlink to AG_ArmourMajor
		more than once on VU_Hellguard"): MMMM Convergence - Genetics swaps BS_NaturalArmor for AG_ArmourMajor, so when
		it loads first the hellguard already had the gene and this plain add gave it a second copy.
	-->
	<Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
		<xpath>Defs/XenotypeDef[defName="VU_Succubus"][not(genes/li[text()="AG_ArmourMedium"])]/genes</xpath>
		<match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
			<xpath>Defs/XenotypeDef[defName="VU_Succubus"][not(genes/li[text()="AG_ArmourMedium"])]/genes</xpath>
			<value>
				<li>AG_ArmourMedium</li>
			</value>
		</match>
	</Operation>
	<Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
		<xpath>Defs/XenotypeDef[defName="VU_Hellguard"][not(genes/li[text()="AG_ArmourMajor"])]/genes</xpath>
		<match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
			<xpath>Defs/XenotypeDef[defName="VU_Hellguard"][not(genes/li[text()="AG_ArmourMajor"])]/genes</xpath>
			<value>
				<li>AG_ArmourMajor</li>
			</value>
		</match>
	</Operation>

</Patch>
